  "body": "Source finding, not a measured attack. `each.rs::hash_held` (next fbfb319f/ddb7199d, and released main 6e0dffd3 line 152) partitions a turn's held hashers with `hashers[i].core.key == key && flags == flags`.\n\nFor keyed hashing that compares secret keys:\n\n- `[u32; 8] ==` may stop at the first differing word, so its time can depend on how many leading key words match;\n- the result chooses the work: hashers whose keys equal the first held hasher's hash together, the rest in a later pass. Turn time therefore depends on key equality, a larger signal than the comparison itself.\n\nA cursory reader keying one Hasher per tenant or per connection (`Mode::Keyed`) and calling `update_each` sees nothing in the docs about key-dependent timing. #267 states the intended contract: \"Control flow and memory access depend on public input shapes, independently of key and message values.\" Plausible harm: a tenant who controls their own key and can time shared turns obtains an equality oracle against co-resident keys. Prefix leakage through the comparison is smaller and noisier.\n\nI have not measured timing or built an attack; severity rests on the contract. Options, your call: `constant_time_eq` (already a dependency) for the comparison, which removes the prefix signal but keeps the equality-dependent grouping; documenting that `update_each`'s speed reveals whether hashers share a key; or grouping by something public. #281 and #280 are the mixed-key work; I have not changed them.\n\n\u2014 Sam Shackleton",
